{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'browser-cmd text'","aggregated_output":"<browser trusted=\"no\">\nURL: https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/150550/foolproof-chocolate-fudge/\n\n[Skipped site header, footer — `text full=true` reads them]\nRecipes\nTrusted Brands: Recipes and Tips\nEAGLE BRAND®\n# Foolproof Chocolate Fudge\n4.4\n(250)\n194 Reviews\n19 Photos\nThis classic and truly foolproof fudge recipe will be a favorite for years to come. Try one of our suggested variations or personalize the fudge by adding your favorite ingredients to the basic recipe. Fudge also makes a great homemade gift to share with family and friends.\nSubmitted by\nEagle brand\nUpdated on August 7, 2026\nSave\nRate\nPrint\nShare\nAdd Photo\n19\nServings:\n32\nYield:\n2 pounds\nJump to Nutrition Facts\n### WHY YOU’LL LOVE THIS RECIPE\nTrue to its name, this rich fudge is hard to mess up with just five ingredients and three easy steps.\nHome cooks like to bring these fudge squares to potlucks and also gift them during the holidays.\nReviewer MelodieW writes, “It comes out creamy every time and it’s not grainy at all.”\nKeep Screen Awake\n## Ingredients\n1/2x\n[Selected: 1x]\n1x\n2x\nOriginal recipe (1X) yields 32 servings\n3 cups semi-sweet chocolate chips\n1 (14 ounce) can EAGLE BRAND® Sweetened Condensed Milk\n1 dash Dash salt\n¾ cup chopped nuts\n1 ½ teaspoons vanilla extract\n## Directions\nIn heavy saucepan, over low heat, melt chocolate chips with sweetened condensed milk and salt. Remove from heat; stir in nuts (optional) and vanilla.\nSpread evenly into wax-paper-lined 8- or 9-inch square pan. Chill 2 hours or until firm.\nLife fudge out of pan and place onto cutting board; peel off paper and cut into squares. Store covered in refrigerator.\n## Variations\nCreamy Dark Chocolate Fudge: Melt 2 cups miniature marshmallows with chocolate chips and sweetened condensed milk. Proceed as above.\nMilk Chocolate Fudge: Omit 1 cup semi-sweet chocolate chips. Add 1 cup milk chocolate chips. Proceed as above.\nRocky Road Fudge: Omit 1 cup semi-sweet chocolate chips, salt, nuts and vanilla. In saucepan, melt chocolate chips with sweetened condensed milk and 2 tablespoons butter or margarine. In large bowl, combine 2 cups dry-roasted peanuts and 1 (10 1/2-ounce) package miniature marshmallows. Stir in chocolate mixture. Spread in wax paper-lined 13x9-inch pan. Proceed as above. (Makes about 2 3/4 pounds)\nMicrowave: In 1-quart glass measure, combine chocolate chips with sweetened condensed milk and salt. Cook on HIGH (100% power) 3 minutes or until chips melt, stirring after 1 1/2 minutes. Stir in remaining ingredients. Proceed as above.\n## Nutrition Facts (per serving)\n[Table]\n146 | Calories\n7g | Fat\n14g | Carbs\n2g | Protein\n[End table]\nShow Full Nutrition Label\nCook this recipe and more in the MyRecipes app.\nGet the App\nSave\nRate\nPrint\n448\nhome cooks made it!\nI Made It\n## Ask the Community\nGet recipe help and connect with the community\nAsk the first question\n## Reviews (194)\nCheck out our Community Guidelines about reviews.\nFoolproof Chocolate Fudge\nMy Rating\nRate this a 1\nRate this a 2\nRate this a 3\nRate this a 4\nRate this a 5\nMy Review\nCancel\nSubmit\n4.4 out of 5\n250 Ratings\n5 star\n170\n4 star\n45\n3 star\n15\n2 star\n12\n1 star\n8\n448\n home cooks made it!\nMost helpful positive review\nJoni\n12/22/2007\nA small tip - after chilling for 2 hrs this is very hard to get out of the pan. Put a couple of inches of hot water in your sink and let the pan sit in it for 15 minutes. You can then flip it over and it will pop right out.\n498\nReply\n### Featured Tweaks\n12116\n12/11/2013\nThis is the recipe for fudge my mom made and we've loved through the years. I add 1 cup milk chocolate chips and 1 T of corn syrup to make a smoother taste and texture. I like to make half a batch just with nuts and half a batch with rum-soaked raisins and nuts.\nTwo tips:\n1. I line a glass container with aluminum foil will extra foil on the edges to help lift the fudge out.\n2. When the fudge is lightly set I take a pizza cutter and cut my pieces then let it set fully. When I'm ready to serve it, it is already evenly scored and it comes apart neatly.\nThis is a wonderful, not too sweet, fudge to make with children, too.\nRead More\n18\npumpkinsmom\n12/21/2015\nI did 1 cup dark chocolate chunks and 2 cups semi-sweet chocolate chips and substituted peppermint extract for the vanilla (in equal measure). I used a double boiler and melted the ingredients until they were just barely all soft and mixed then took them off the heat immediately. My husband said this is the best fudge he's ever had - not too sweet, just the right consistency. This will be a Christmas staple!\nRead More\n0\nSandy Jo\n12/15/2013\nJust made these and loved them. I am a dark chocolate lover so I used Gharadelli Dark Chocolate Chips. I used chopped pecans and melted the chips and milk in a pyrex in the microwave, worked wonderfully. I sprinkled a few crushed peppermint pieces on top after spreading it into the dish for a lovely mint touch (good for Christmas). I also lined my dish with foil, leaving some hanging over the edge and sprayed it lightly with oil. It was a snap to lift from the dish, put on a cutting board and cut into any size piece desired!\nRead More\n6\nJoanE\n12/16/2012\nThe second time I made this recipe, I made two batches. I used a 9x13\" pan. I used dark chocolate, ghirardelli 60% choc. chips for the first batch. I spread it on the bottom of the pan. Then, I made a batch with ghirardelli milk chocolate chips,and spread it on top of the dark. The two types of chocolate, layered like that, with the contrasting flavors of dark and milk chocolate in each bite is tantalizing to the taste buds! My family and neighbors love it! I do have some problems with the dark choc. mixture becoming grainy. Will try 16oz. instead of 18 next time. The milk choc has been perfect each time.\nSuggestions on why this is happening are most welcome!\nRead More\n3\nMina Taylor\n12/25/2016\nNote the 2nd positive review: \"I use one bag go milk chocolate chips and add 1/2 bag of semi-sweet also. This leaves a very nice creamy texture. Here's a little tip that everyone loves. Freeze the remaining 1/2 bag of semi-sweet chocolate chips. At the end of stirring, pour in the frozen chocolate chips, give the mix one good, quick, final stir, pour into pan and refrigerate. (I like it cold!) The mixture is hot enough to melt part, but not all, of the frozen chips. It will leave tiny chocolate chunks throughout. Want another tip? After preparing as I did above, add one cup of peanut butter to this recipe before the final stirring and refrigerate. Mmmm!! (If adding the frozen chocolate chips, always add them last to prevent them from melting totally.) Having trouble getting it out of the pan? Line the pan with foil. After it sets, simply lift it out, remove the foil, and place the fudge on a dish or cutting surface to cut.\"\nRead More\n0\nmslisa murphy\n02/03/2018\nDelicious and absolutely full proof. This is also a great starter recipe for young cooks. You’re not “cooking” so much as warming slowly. My husband is the only family member who likes nuts in the fudge,so I do half with pecans (roast them for 15 minutes @ 325 with a pinch of salt for extra flavor ) and the kids like mini marshmallows.\nI’ve made this for so long,people just expect it. This fudge recipe along with Eagle Brand 7 layer bars are perfect small but sweet treats\nRead More\n0\nSher\n12/16/2011\nThis is an easy quick fudge recipe that will never turn out grainy. I have found that I get an overly thick mess if I use 3 cups chocolate chips, as another reviewer found. I use 2 or 2 1/2 cups of chips instead, and it works out much better. I also microwave the sweetened condenced milk in the microwave before adding the chips, then pour them in and stir until melted.\nRead More\n17\nJoan Molling\n12/20/2014\nI used a mocha, salted caramel version. 2 c. semi-sweet chips melted with 1 c milk chocolate chips along with the can of sweetened cond. milk and 1 t vanilla, 1 t instant espresso powder dissolved in 2 T half and half. Melt stir till smooth and pour in 8\" foil lined pan. Meanwhile, melt 1 c caramel bits with 1 T half and half. Pour over fudge in pan and swirl with a knife. Sprinkle with a bit of coarse sea salt. Just gilded the lily a little :)\nRead More\n1\nSandraB77\n12/27/2015\nThis fudge is so delicious and simple! Great for a quick sweet treat. I've made it twice in the last week, the first time-exactly as written. The second time I was short on semi-sweet chips, so used two cups semi and one cup milk chocolate chips. Be sure to use good quality chips, as the chocolate is the main focal point. With the second batch, I did not stir the nuts in, but after pouring the fudge in the pan, I sprinkled the top with chopped pecans and toffee chips, and pressed it in so it would stick, before placing fudge in fridge to set. I placed each square in a mini baking cup and stacked it on a pretty tray. Everyone loved it! No one knows how simple it was to make ;D\nRead More\n0\nCarol Van Gorp\n12/20/2019\nI had some pecans soaked in Kentucky Bourbon that I used in my fudge. Wow! It was fabulous and so much easier than making Bourbon balls. Think this is going to be a holiday tradition. I did add a little Bourbon to the chocolate. We don’t have any children around so it was okay.\nRead More\n1\n194 Reviews\nSort\nFilter\nLinda\n05/20/2026\nMade this tonight. Followed suggestion of some reviewers to add a bit of butter. That did not look appealing but the result was delicious.\n0\nReply\npat\n01/31/2026\nA quick and easy dessert to make when the grandkids visit. They love it!\n0\nReply\nShay\n12/17/2025\nDid not work\nI've made fudge for years and knew something was immediately off when I saw the chocolate and the cocoa butter separation. I stirred this almost constantly and easy before it reached soft ball stage it was funky. I followed through and finished with the rest of the add ins (rocky road) but now I'm stuck with $15 of wasted ingredients. Yes, I used a heavy sauce pan and no it wasn't over cooked. It never even reached 150°. Definitely going back to my old recipe.\nRead More\n0\nReply\nView Replies (2)\nJayna\n12/04/2025\nFamily favorite\nRecipe passed down from my Grandmother. We've made it perfectly hundreds of times. The only time it wasn't great was when I used a general brand butter. I found out general brand butter has more water and less fat which makes a huge.\n0\nReply\nSandra Mathews Freeman\n12/21/2024\nFamily favorite\nI have made this fudge for many years. It is smooth and has the perfect taste.\n1\nReply\nRiley\n02/04/2022\nEasy and quick. Good directions. Edited\n0\nReply\nTuxedoville\n12/20/2020\nMake it every Christmas. Delicious, easy, can’t go wrong.\n0\nReply\nBuffy De Carlo\n01/13/2020\nThis was the first time that I ever made fudge and it was Amazing! I added 2 Tbls of butter like someone suggested and stirred it really well until nice and smooth. I added walnuts and took it to work and everyone absolutely Loved it! Thank you for this easy foolproof recipe. This will be my new tradition for years to come!\n1\nReply\nmpathhealr\n07/27/2019\nI learned to make fudge using the semi sweet bars, sugar, milk, corn syrup... And beating it until t lost or maybe gained glossiness. This is just as good, simpler, and far more versatile. My adult children look forward to the many variations we have devised. Try drained and chopped maraschino cherries mixed in, or add instant coffee, almond extract, cherry extract, mix in pnut butter early for pnutbutter fudge.\nRead More\n2\nReply\nLoad More reviews\n## Most-Saved Recipes Like This\nNo Fail Chocolate Fudge\n34\nSave\nCreamy Low-Fat Chocolate Fudge\n18\n3 hrs 10 mins\nSave\nBest Ever Fudge\n40\nSave\nAunt Teen’s Creamy Chocolate Fudge\n2,465\n2 hrs 30 mins\nSave\nMocha Fudge\n15\n25 mins\nSave\nCookies ‘n’ Creme Fudge\n362\n2 hrs 15 mins\nSave\n3-Minute Fudge\n21\n3 hrs 8 mins\nSave\nMillion Dollar Fudge\n222\n3 hrs 30 mins\nSave\nDark Chocolate Peppermint Fudge Recipe\n18\n1 hr 15 mins\nSave\nMom's Christmas Fudge\n4\n2 hrs 20 mins\nSave\n## You’ll Also Love\nChocolate Peanut Butter Swirl Fudge\n54\nRatings\nCreamy Eggnog Fudge\n70\nRatings\nLayered Mint Chocolate Fudge\n163\nRatings\nEagle Brand Chocolate Truffles\n27\nRatings\nChocolate Walnut Fudge\n115\nRatings\nThe Original Fantasy Fudge\n524\nRatings\nToll House Famous Fudge\n44\nRatings\nMicrowave Peanut Butter Chocolate Swirl Fudge\n7\nRatings\nCreamy Low-Fat Chocolate Fudge\n18\nRatings\nFudge\n1,793\nRatings\nEagle Brand Peanut Butter Fudge\n116\nRatings\nDark Chocolate Peppermint Fudge Recipe\n18\nRatings\nMillion Dollar Fudge\n222\nRatings\nChocolate Orange Fudge\n60\nRatings\nIrish Cream Truffle Fudge\n289\nRatings\nPumpkin Fudge\n358\nRatings\n--- frame: about:blank ---\n\n--- frame: about:blank ---\n\nImage descriptions: Creamy Guilt-Free Fudge · Squares of creamy chocolate fudge with nuts on a white plate. · close up view of a pile of Cookies 'n' Creme Fudge · A stack of chocolate fudge pieces with nuts served on a plate · close up view of pieces of Layered Mint Chocolate Fudge on a plate · Eagle Brand® Chocolate Truffles · A large serving plate of The Original Fantasy Fudge, cut into squares and stacked · a low angle view of a big pile of chocolate fudge on a red plate · a low angle, close up view of a pile of peanut butter fudge squares stacked on a plate with a bowl of crushed peanuts sitting nearby. · Bowl of pumpkin fudge cut into squares.\n</browser>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
