{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > NOTES.md <<'EOF'\nChosen recipe: Aunt Teen’s Creamy Chocolate Fudge\nURL: https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/15821/aunt-teens-creamy-chocolate-fudge/\nAllrecipes page text: “Desserts”; “Prep Time: 10 mins”; “4.7 out of 5”; “2465 Ratings”; “2 cups milk chocolate chips”; “1 cup semisweet chocolate chips”.\nCook Time: 20 mins; Additional Time: 2 hrs; Total Time: 2 hrs 30 mins. Original recipe yields 48 servings, one 8x8-inch pan. Updated January 22, 2026.\nEOF\ncat > ANSWER.txt <<'EOF'\nFINAL: Aunt Teen’s Creamy Chocolate Fudge\n\nChosen Allrecipes dessert: prep time 10 minutes (less than 30), rated 4.7/5 from 2,465 ratings, and made with milk chocolate and semisweet chocolate chips. Makes 48 servings in one 8-inch square pan. Cook time: 20 minutes; chilling: 2 hours; total: 2 hours 30 minutes.\n\nIngredients\n- 1½ cups white sugar\n- One 7-ounce jar marshmallow creme\n- ⅔ cup evaporated milk\n- ¼ cup butter\n- ¼ teaspoon salt\n- 2 cups milk chocolate chips\n- 1 cup semisweet chocolate chips\n- ½ cup chopped nuts\n- 1 teaspoon vanilla extract\n\nInstructions\n1. Assemble the ingredients and line an 8-inch square pan with aluminum foil.\n2. In a large saucepan over medium heat, combine the sugar, marshmallow creme, evaporated milk, butter, and salt. Bring to a full boil, then cook for 5 minutes while stirring continuously.\n3. Take the saucepan off the heat. Add both kinds of chocolate chips and stir until melted and smooth. Mix in the nuts and vanilla.\n4. Transfer the mixture to the lined pan. Refrigerate for about 2 hours, until firm.\n\nSource: Allrecipes, “Aunt Teen’s Creamy Chocolate Fudge,” submitted by Kelly Phillips, updated January 22, 2026.\nhttps://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/15821/aunt-teens-creamy-chocolate-fudge/\nEvidence: final.png.\nEOF\nbrowser-cmd click @e7ex.27\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
