{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > ANSWER.txt <<'EOF'\nFINAL: Chocolate Walnut Fudge\n\nThis Allrecipes dessert has a 10-minute prep time, a 4.2/5 user rating from 115 ratings, and semisweet chocolate chips. Makes 36 servings in an 8-inch square dish. The page lists 15 minutes cooking time and 2 hours total time.\n\nIngredients\n- ½ cup butter\n- 1 cup semisweet chocolate chips\n- 1 teaspoon vanilla extract\n- 2 cups white sugar\n- 5 ounces evaporated milk\n- 10 large marshmallows\n- 1 cup chopped walnuts\n\nInstructions\n1. Butter an 8-inch square dish.\n2. Put the butter, chocolate chips, and vanilla in a mixing bowl; set aside.\n3. In a medium saucepan over medium heat, combine the sugar, evaporated milk, and marshmallows. Stir frequently as you bring it to a boil. Lower the heat and cook for another 6 minutes, stirring continuously, then remove from the heat.\n4. Pour the hot marshmallow mixture into the mixing bowl. Beat until the mixture thickens and becomes matte. Quickly fold in the walnuts and transfer to the buttered dish. Refrigerate for several hours, until firm.\n\nSource: Allrecipes, “Chocolate Walnut Fudge,” submitted by Amber, updated May 28, 2026.\nhttps://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/23268/chocolate-walnut-fudge/\nEOF\ncat >> NOTES.md <<'EOF'\nFinal selection: Chocolate Walnut Fudge\nURL: https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/23268/chocolate-walnut-fudge/\nPage text: “Desserts”; “Prep Time: 10 mins”; “4.2 out of 5”; “115 Ratings”; “1 cup semisweet chocolate chips”.\nOriginal 1X yields 36 servings. Cook Time 15 mins; Additional Time 1 hr 35 mins; Total Time 2 hrs. Updated May 28, 2026.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > ANSWER.txt <<'EOF'\nFINAL: Chocolate Walnut Fudge\n\nThis Allrecipes dessert has a 10-minute prep time, a 4.2/5 user rating from 115 ratings, and semisweet chocolate chips. Makes 36 servings in an 8-inch square dish. The page lists 15 minutes cooking time and 2 hours total time.\n\nIngredients\n- ½ cup butter\n- 1 cup semisweet chocolate chips\n- 1 teaspoon vanilla extract\n- 2 cups white sugar\n- 5 ounces evaporated milk\n- 10 large marshmallows\n- 1 cup chopped walnuts\n\nInstructions\n1. Butter an 8-inch square dish.\n2. Put the butter, chocolate chips, and vanilla in a mixing bowl; set aside.\n3. In a medium saucepan over medium heat, combine the sugar, evaporated milk, and marshmallows. Stir frequently as you bring it to a boil. Lower the heat and cook for another 6 minutes, stirring continuously, then remove from the heat.\n4. Pour the hot marshmallow mixture into the mixing bowl. Beat until the mixture thickens and becomes matte. Quickly fold in the walnuts and transfer to the buttered dish. Refrigerate for several hours, until firm.\n\nSource: Allrecipes, “Chocolate Walnut Fudge,” submitted by Amber, updated May 28, 2026.\nhttps://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/23268/chocolate-walnut-fudge/\nEOF\ncat >> NOTES.md <<'EOF'\nFinal selection: Chocolate Walnut Fudge\nURL: https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/23268/chocolate-walnut-fudge/\nPage text: “Desserts”; “Prep Time: 10 mins”; “4.2 out of 5”; “115 Ratings”; “1 cup semisweet chocolate chips”.\nOriginal 1X yields 36 servings. Cook Time 15 mins; Additional Time 1 hr 35 mins; Total Time 2 hrs. Updated May 28, 2026.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
