{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > ANSWER.txt <<'EOF'\nFINAL: Chocolate Walnut Fudge\n\nAllrecipes lists a 10-minute prep time, a user rating of 4.2/5 from 115 ratings, and semisweet chocolate chips. This dessert makes 36 servings in an 8-inch square dish. Listed cook time: 15 minutes; total time: 2 hours.\n\nIngredients\n- ½ cup butter\n- 1 cup semisweet chocolate chips\n- 1 teaspoon vanilla extract\n- 2 cups white sugar\n- 5 ounces evaporated milk\n- 10 large marshmallows\n- 1 cup chopped walnuts\n\nInstructions\n1. Butter an 8-inch square dish.\n2. Set aside a mixing bowl containing the butter, chocolate chips, and vanilla.\n3. Combine sugar, evaporated milk, and marshmallows in a medium saucepan over medium heat. Bring to a boil, stirring frequently. Reduce heat to low; cook another 6 minutes, stirring constantly. Remove from heat.\n4. Pour the marshmallow mixture into the mixing bowl. Beat until thickened and no longer shiny. Quickly fold in walnuts and pour into the buttered dish. Refrigerate for several hours until firm.\n\nSource: Allrecipes, “Chocolate Walnut Fudge,” submitted by Amber, updated May 28, 2026.\nhttps://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/23268/chocolate-walnut-fudge/\n\nEvidence: final.png shows the name, rating, prep time, complete ingredients, and four directions. Verified October 27, 2026.\nEOF\ncat >> NOTES.md <<'EOF'\n\nComplete ingredient and direction verification, October 27, 2026:\nSource opened in browser-cmd, active tab t3: https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/23268/chocolate-walnut-fudge/\nOriginal recipe 1X, 36 servings.\nIngredients as rendered:\n½ cup butter\n1 cup semisweet chocolate chips\n1 teaspoon vanilla extract\n2 cups white sugar\n5 ounces evaporated milk\n10 large marshmallows\n1 cup chopped walnuts\nDirections as rendered:\n1. Butter an 8x8 inch dish.\n2. Place butter, chocolate chips and vanilla in a mixing bowl. Set aside.\n3. In a medium saucepan over medium 